## Introduction

<br>

Creating cohorts from scratch using R. Workflow overview:

<br>

::::::::::: columns
:::: {.column .fragment width="25%"}
### 1. Drug codelists

Creating codelists

::: text-center
**↓**

[`CodelistGenerator`](https://github.com/darwin-eu/CodelistGenerator)
:::
::::

::: {.column .fragment .arrow-column width="6%"}
<br> **→**
:::

:::: {.column .fragment width="25%"}
### 2. Drug cohorts

Codelists + cohort logic

::: text-center
**↓**

[`CohortConstructor`](https://github.com/OHDSI/CohortConstructor)
:::
::::

::: {.column .fragment .arrow-column width="6%"}
<br> **→**
:::

:::: {.column .fragment width="37%"}
### 3. Diagnostics

Reviewing codelists and cohorts

::: text-center
**↓**

[`PhenotypeR`](https://github.com/OHDSI/PhenotypeR)
:::
::::
:::::::::::


## What cohorts are we going to create?

<br>

:::::: {.columns}

::: {.column .fragment width="26%"}
### Amoxicillin

1. Drug ingredient of amoxicillin and descendants
2. Collapse gaps less or equal to a week
3. First ever exposure
4. Require to be adults (≥ 18 years)
:::

::: {.column width="6%"}
:::

::: {.column .fragment width="26%"}
### Amoxicillin oral route

1. Drug ingredient of amoxicillin and descendants but only with oral route
2. Collapse gaps less or equal to a week
3. First ever exposure
4. Require to be adults (≥ 18 years)
:::

::: {.column width="6%"}
:::

::: {.column .fragment width="29%"}
### Amoxicillin + clavulanate combination oral route

1. Drug ingredient of amoxicillin and descendants but only with oral route
2. Collapse gaps less or equal to a week
3. First ever exposure
4. Require to be adults (≥ 18 years)
:::

::::::

# Step 1: Creating codelists

## Create CDM reference

1)  Load relevant packages

. . .



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(omopgenerics)
library(omock)
library(CodelistGenerator)
library(CohortConstructor)
library(CohortCharacteristics)
library(PhenotypeR)
library(here)
library(duckdb)
library(visOmopResults)
library(gt)
library(purrr)
library(dplyr)
```
:::



2)  Create a cdm reference to a synthetic omop database

. . .



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
cdm <- omock::mockCdmFromDataset("delphi-100k",
                                 source = "duckdb")
```
:::



## Create CDM reference

<br>

The `cdm` object provides a reference to the tables in our data source.

We can access individual tables using `$`. For example, to access the OMOP `concept` table:



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
cdm$concept
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
# A query:  ?? x 10
# Database: DuckDB 1.5.6 [root@Darwin 25.6.0:R 4.4.3//private/var/folders/sw/rd8zn92n2nz45cfcc5dcs_080000gr/T/Rtmpja4ogG/filee66b77c20880.duckdb]
   concept_id concept_name              domain_id vocabulary_id concept_class_id
        <int> <chr>                     <chr>     <chr>         <chr>           
 1   44565804 OCTINOXATE / OXYBENZONE … Drug      DPD           Branded Drug Fo…
 2   44675452 OCTINOXATE / OXYBENZONE … Drug      DPD           Branded Drug Fo…
 3   44675453 OCTINOXATE / OXYBENZONE … Drug      DPD           Branded Drug Fo…
 4   44666854 OCTINOXATE 7% / OXYBENZO… Drug      DPD           Clinical Drug   
 5   44633022 OCTINOXATE 3.75% / OXYBE… Drug      DPD           Clinical Drug   
 6   44658398 OCTINOXATE 6% / OXYBENZO… Drug      DPD           Clinical Drug   
 7   44557377 2-PHENYLBENZIMIDAZOLE-5-… Drug      DPD           Clinical Drug   
 8   44633023 AVOBENZONE 1% / OCTINOXA… Drug      DPD           Branded Drug Co…
 9   44574224 AVOBENZONE 2.5% / OCTINO… Drug      DPD           Branded Drug Co…
